    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.05) anchoring our lineup. **Jacob Wilson** occupies the most favorable spot, leveraging a premier leadoff role against the soft matchup of Valdez, while **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a massive 19% efficiency boost provided by the matchup against Mikolas. **Jackson Merrill** (69.25) remains a must-start, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Mahle provides one of the highest ceiling outcomes in our outfield. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough arm in S\u00e1nchez (2.84 xERA), his 16% park factor cushion keeps him in the mix, though his output is slightly dampened by a catcher who suppresses steal attempts\u2014a critical consideration given our strategy to emphasize speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Denzer Guzman**, who landed just outside our starting criteria with a 44.36 score. While his platoon edge is solid, the optimizer favored the higher-upside profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose roles in the 7-8 spots are mitigated by the favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez. We are opting to bench **Miguel Vargas** (39.08) entirely, as he falls below our \"Zebras Floor\" due to his unfavorable matchup against Rasmussen. As we monitor the board, keep a close eye on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; his 64.59 score reflects a strong 7% platoon advantage, but his performance against Mathews will be a barometer for the team's overall scoring efficiency. Finally, ensure the status of **Kyle Tucker** and **Jordan Westburg** is noted; their continued absence from the lineup significantly restricts our bench depth, putting added pressure on our active starters to maintain our category standings.",
